#
# Give the server a liveness heartbeat. Its probes checked for an
# established connection to the bridge, which a frozen server keeps:
# frozen, it stayed Ready for four minutes and was replaced after about
# five and a half (#33). The supervising parent now waits for its
# request child a second at a time and rewrites a heartbeat between
# slices, withheld while that child is stopped or has held no bridge
# connection for fifty seconds - the double-TLS teardown wedge the old
# probe was the backstop for, still replaced within its two minutes. A
# pidfd ends each slice as soon as the child exits, so the wait adds
# nothing to a request. See patches/README.md.
#
